268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 804 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, an IR sensor is connected to pin 2 \(IR_PIN\), a buzzer to pin 5 \(BUZZ_PIN\), and an LED to pin 6 \(LED_PIN\). The LED works in the opposite way to the buzzer.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 805 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the IR sensor as INPUT and both the buzzer and LED as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, both are turned OFF.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 806 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the IR sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in IRState.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 807 0 R
/E (If an object is detected \(LOW signal\), the buzzer turns ON and the LED turns OFF. If no object is detected \(HIGH\), the buzzer turns OFF and the LED turns ON.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (So overall, the system detects objects using the IR sensor and controls the buzzer and LED in opposite ways.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
