<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 835 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, an IR sensor is connected to pin 2 \(IR_PIN\), and two LEDs are connected to pins 5 \(LED_DETECTED\) and 6 \(LED_IDLE\). One LED shows detection, and the other shows idle status.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 836 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the IR sensor as INPUT and both LEDs as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). Initially, the detected LED is OFF and the idle LED is ON.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 837 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the IR sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in irState)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
